For glibc’s `struct printf_info`:

| Format component | No `*` specified | When specified as `*` in the **arginfo function** | When specified as `*` in the **handler function** |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| `info->width` | `0` if omitted | `INT_MIN` | Actual `int` value retrieved from the argument list |
| `info->prec` | `-1` if omitted | `INT_MIN` | Actual `int` value retrieved from the argument list |

Thus, the arginfo function can detect a star by testing:

```c
if (info->width == INT_MIN) {
    /* width comes from an argument */
}

if (info->prec == INT_MIN) {
    /* precision comes from an argument */
}
```

The arginfo function must return the number of arguments expected by the conversion and fill the `argtypes` array with their types. The handler receives the resolved width and precision values. ([Conversion Specifier Options](https://sourceware.org/glibc/manual/latest/html_node/Conversion-Specifier-Options.html), [Defining the Output Handler](https://www.sourceware.org/glibc/manual/latest/html_node/Defining-the-Output-Handler.html))
